 on conquering  Westeros with his bloodthirsty khalasar  their methods weren't dissimilar to  those of the Mongol hordes led by famed  Emperor Genghis Khan both led armies of  fearsome mounted warriors who raped  pillaged and murdered their way through  anything that stood in their way but the  similarities don't end there  you may recall the grisly end of Viserys  Targaryen who had a vat of molten gold  poured over his head well it's not  dissimilar to how the governor of atre  met his maker after royally pissing off  genghis khan by killing a whole load of  his men khan had the governor executed  by pouring molten silver into his eyes  and mouth and you thought that pizza  burn was bad  season threes red wedding is one of the  most infamous events in Westeros in one  fell swoop Tywin Lannister Walder Frey  and Roose Bolton managed to take a whole  bunch of thorns out from their side in  particular the upstart King in the north  Robb Stark Walder Frey's treachery was  all the worse because he broke guessed  right an ancient custom that once  invoked guaranteed that neither host nor  guests could harm each other for the  duration that the guest was staying such  hospitality laws actually existed and  Martin has spoken in the past about how  he took inspiration from two specific  events the black dinner and the Glencoe  massacre the black dinner involved the  murder of the 16 year old Earl of  Douglas and his younger brother the  brothers were invited to dine with the  10 year old King James ii of scotland  but it was all a trick and during dinner  a black bull's head a symbol of death  was brought in and placed upon the table  the brothers were then taken outside and  promptly executed the Glencoe massacre  of 1692 had a much larger body count  clan Campbell were guests a rival clan  MacDonald and putting their differences  aside  they brought soldiers and stayed under  the roof of their enemy for ten days and  nights clan Campbell accepted the  hospitality of the M